torrent-vpn-waiting = Les torrents démarrent une fois le contrôle VPN validé. { $reason }

# Note on the sources screen: the VPN guard has no verdict yet.
torrent-vpn-unverified = Les torrents démarrent une fois le contrôle VPN validé. La connexion n’a pas encore été vérifiée.

# Error: the torrent session did not start because the interface closed first.
torrent-interface-closed = anistream s’est fermé avant le démarrage des torrents.

# Error: the torrent session could not start. The reason comes from the torrent engine.
torrent-session-failed = Impossible de démarrer la session torrent. { $reason }

# Toast when torrents are up but no operating-system firewall rule backs the VPN guard. Terminal only: the engine never sends it to the apps.
torrent-no-kill-switch = Rien sur cet appareil n’arrête le trafic torrent si le VPN tombe. Lancez « anistream --doctor » pour le configurer.

# Toast when the connection check could not run. The reason comes from the VPN settings.
torrent-not-checked = Impossible de vérifier la connexion. { $reason }

# Note on the sources screen after the source chain is rebuilt with torrents on.
sources-reloaded-torrents-pending = Sources rechargées. Les torrents démarrent une fois le contrôle VPN validé.

# Note on the sources screen after the source chain is rebuilt with torrents off.
sources-reloaded-torrents-off = Torrents désactivés. La session a été arrêtée.

# Note on a running job: requests to AniList are being slowed to stay within its limit. A countdown follows.
job-anilist-limit = En attente de la limite de requêtes d’AniList

# Toast when there is no job to carry the wait for AniList's rate limit.
notice-anilist-limit = Attente de { $wait } à cause de la limite d’AniList.

# Toast when the AniList fallback takes over because AniList cannot be reached.
notice-anilist-unreachable = AniList ne répond pas. Affichage des données d’un autre service pour l’instant.

# Toast when no metadata service answered and the last cached data is shown.
notice-metadata-cached = Aucun service de métadonnées n’a répondu. Affichage des dernières données en cache.

# Toast when AniList answers again.
notice-anilist-back = AniList est de nouveau disponible.

# Toast when a command needs watch parties but this app was built without them.
notice-party-not-built = Visionnages en groupe ne sont pas inclus dans cette application.

# Toast after a tracker sign-in succeeded. The tracker is its name, such as AniList.
notice-signed-in = Connecté à { $tracker }.

# Toast after a sign-in succeeded and the token went into the system keychain.
notice-signed-in-keychain = Connecté à { $tracker }. Le jeton est enregistré dans le trousseau du système.

# Toast after a sign-in succeeded on a device with no keychain. The token is in a file only this user can read. It is said so that someone on a shared computer knows.
notice-signed-in-file = Connecté à { $tracker }. Aucun trousseau n'est disponible, donc le jeton est dans un fichier privé sur cet appareil.

# Toast when a sign-in worked but the token could not be stored. The reason comes from the system.
notice-signed-in-unsaved = Connecté à { $tracker }, mais le jeton n'a pas été enregistré. Il faudra vous reconnecter la prochaine fois. { $reason }

# Toast when a sign-in token could not be stored. The reason comes from the system.
notice-token-not-saved = Impossible d'enregistrer le jeton de connexion. Essayez de vous reconnecter. { $reason }

# Toast when a sign-in did not finish. The reason comes from the tracker or the network.
notice-sign-in-failed = Impossible de vous connecter à { $tracker }. Réessayez. { $reason }

# Toast when the wait for a sign-in ended early. The reason comes from the system.
notice-sign-in-stopped = La connexion à { $tracker } s'est arrêtée avant la fin. Réessayez. { $reason }

# Toast when a tracker would not give a token for the sign-in. The reason comes from the tracker.
notice-token-exchange-failed = Impossible d'obtenir un jeton de { $tracker }. Essayez de vous reconnecter. { $reason }

# Toast when no browser could be opened for a sign-in. The reason comes from the system.
notice-browser-not-opened = Impossible d'ouvrir un navigateur pour la connexion. Vérifiez qu'un navigateur est installé, puis réessayez. { $reason }

# Toast when a sign-in redirect arrives and no sign-in is waiting for it.
notice-sign-in-not-waiting = Aucune connexion à { $tracker } n'attend cette réponse. Recommencez la connexion.

# Toast when a sign-in redirect does not match the request that was made.
notice-sign-in-wrong-request = La connexion à { $tracker } ne correspond pas à la demande faite. Recommencez la connexion.

# Toast when a tracker sent the person back without a token.
notice-sign-in-no-token = La connexion à { $tracker } est revenue sans jeton. Réessayez.

# Toast when this build has no MyAnimeList client to finish a sign-in with.
notice-mal-client-missing-build = Impossible de finir la connexion à MyAnimeList : cette version n'a pas de client pour elle.

# Toast on a screen that opens Kitsu's sign-in as a prompt. It is shown with a button to open it.
notice-kitsu-signs-in-on-accounts = Kitsu se connecte depuis l'écran Comptes.

# Toast when a tracker has no way to sign in yet.
notice-sign-in-unsupported = La connexion à { $tracker } n'est pas encore prise en charge.

# Toast on an app that cannot receive a browser redirect.
notice-sign-in-needs-redirect = La connexion à { $tracker } demande une redirection par le navigateur, que cette application ne peut pas recevoir.

# Toast when AniList is set to a sign-in method only the anistream app can finish. The setting name is a key of the config file and is not translated.
notice-anilist-implicit-flow = Cette méthode de connexion AniList ne fonctionne que dans l'application anistream. Pour vous connecter ici, mettez { $setting } à « loopback » dans le fichier de configuration.

# Toast when AniList sign-in needs a client id and secret in the config file. The setting names and the command are not translated.
notice-anilist-client-missing = AniList a besoin d'un identifiant et d'un secret de client. Renseignez { $client } et { $secret } dans le fichier de configuration, puis reconnectez-vous. Pour obtenir l'adresse de connexion, lancez anistream --login-url.

# Toast when AniList is set to paste the code by hand, which a running terminal app cannot take. Terminal only: the engine never sends it to the apps.
notice-anilist-paste-flow = Coller un code n'est pas possible ici. Quittez et lancez anistream --login à la place.

# Toast when MyAnimeList sign-in needs a client id in the config file. The setting name and the address are not translated.
notice-mal-client-missing = MyAnimeList a besoin d'un identifiant de client. Enregistrez une application de type « other » sur myanimelist.net/apiconfig, puis réglez { $setting } dans le fichier de configuration.

# Job note while the browser sign-in is open and the terminal app waits for it to come back.
status-waiting-for-redirect = En attente du retour de { $tracker }…

# Toast when MyAnimeList signed in without a refresh token, so the sign-in lapses in about a month.
notice-mal-no-refresh-token = MyAnimeList n'a pas fourni de jeton de renouvellement. Vous devrez vous reconnecter dans un mois environ.

# Toast when a device-code sign-in needs a client id in the config file. The setting name is a key of the config file and is not translated.
notice-client-id-missing = Réglez d'abord { $setting } dans le fichier de configuration.

# Toast after signing out of a tracker with nothing waiting to send.
notice-signed-out = Déconnecté de { $tracker }.

# Toast after signing out of a tracker. The changes were not discarded: they are sent after the next sign-in.
notice-signed-out-queue =
    { $count ->
        [one] Déconnecté de { $tracker }. Une modification en attente est conservée pour la prochaine connexion.
        [many] Déconnecté de { $tracker }. { $count } modifications en attente sont conservées pour la prochaine connexion.
       *[other] Déconnecté de { $tracker }. { $count } modifications en attente sont conservées pour la prochaine connexion.
    }

# Toast when signing out of a tracker failed. The reason comes from the system.
notice-sign-out-failed = Impossible de vous déconnecter de { $tracker }. Réessayez. { $reason }

# Toast when a setting could not be stored. The cause says why and what to do.
notice-not-saved-because = Impossible d'enregistrer ce réglage. { $cause }

# Toast when the torrent protection choice was saved.
notice-protection-saved = Protection contre les torrents enregistrée.

# Toast when the torrent protection could not be checked. The cause says why.
notice-protection-not-checked = Impossible de vérifier la protection contre les torrents. { $cause }

# Toast when the proxy's password could not be stored. The reason comes from the system.
notice-proxy-password-not-kept = Impossible de conserver le mot de passe du proxy. Saisissez-le à nouveau pour essayer de l'enregistrer. { $reason }

# Toast when a show's setting was given a value it does not take. The value is what was given.
notice-show-setting-refused = Impossible d'enregistrer ce réglage. { $value } n'est pas une valeur valide pour { $setting }.

# Toast when resetting a show's settings failed. The reason comes from the local database.
notice-show-not-reset = Impossible de réinitialiser les réglages de cette série. { $reason }

# Toast when a subtitle choice names subtitles the show has not used.
notice-show-no-such-subtitles = Impossible d'enregistrer ce choix de sous-titres. Cette série n'a pas utilisé ces sous-titres auparavant.

# Toast while torrents are held until the connection check passes.
notice-torrents-waiting-for-check = Les torrents attendent que la vérification de la connexion réussisse de nouveau.

# Toast when the mapping data downloads work again after a failure.
notice-mapping-data-refreshed = Données de correspondance actualisées.

# Toast when the mapping data could not be downloaded. It is said once; the retries are silent.
notice-mapping-data-failed = Impossible d'actualiser les données de correspondance ({ $datasets }). Nouvelle tentative dans { $wait }. { $cause }

# Toast, and desktop notification, for one episode that aired while the app was closed.
notice-episode-aired = { $title }, épisode { $episode }, a été diffusé pendant votre absence.

# Toast, and desktop notification, for several episodes that aired while the app was closed.
notice-episodes-aired =
    { $count ->
        [one] Un nouvel épisode d'une série que vous suivez a été diffusé. Le calendrier l'affiche.
        [many] { $count } nouveaux épisodes de séries que vous suivez ont été diffusés. Le calendrier les affiche.
       *[other] { $count } nouveaux épisodes de séries que vous suivez ont été diffusés. Le calendrier les affiche.
    }

# Toast when a new release of anistream is out, on the terminal app. The command is not translated. Terminal only: the engine never sends it to the apps.
notice-update-available = La version { $tag } est disponible. Lancez anistream --update pour l'installer.

# The reason a setting was refused until the person confirms having no protection.
cause-confirm-no-protection = Confirmez d'abord que vous ne voulez aucune protection.

# The reason a setting was refused until the person confirms the "warn only" choice.
cause-confirm-warn-only = Confirmez d'abord que vous voulez seulement être averti.

# The reason a proxy was refused: it has no host or no port.
cause-proxy-needs-address = Un proxy a besoin d'un hôte et d'un port.

# The reason a proxy could not be checked: its address is not one the check can use.
cause-proxy-address-unusable = L'adresse du proxy ne peut pas être utilisée pour une vérification.

# The reason a request failed: it never reached the server.
cause-server-unreachable = Le serveur est injoignable.

# Toast after a setting is stored. The label is the setting's name.
notice-saved = « { $label } » enregistré.

# Toast when a setting could not be stored. The reason comes from the system.
notice-not-saved = Impossible d’enregistrer ce réglage. { $reason }

# Toast when a title's details did not load.
notice-title-load-failed = Impossible de charger ce titre. Vérifiez votre connexion, puis réessayez.

# Toast when playback stops with an error.
notice-playback-failed = La lecture a échoué. Essayez une autre source.

# Toast when something went wrong inside the engine and it carried on.
notice-engine-fault = Une erreur s’est produite dans anistream. L’application a continué, mais si un écran semble bloqué, quittez-la et ouvrez-la à nouveau.

# Toast at launch when the database was damaged, so a fresh one was started. The path is where the damaged file was moved, kept for recovery. Watch history and downloads start over; what the trackers hold comes back with the next sync.
notice-database-set-aside = La base de données était endommagée, donc anistream en a créé une nouvelle. L’ancien fichier est conservé à { $path }. Vos services de suivi restaurent ce qu’ils contiennent à la prochaine synchronisation.

# Message when anistream could not start because a folder could not be made. The path is the folder, the reason comes from the system.
start-failed-folder = anistream n’a pas pu créer le dossier { $path }. Vérifiez que le disque a de la place et que le dossier est accessible en écriture, puis réessayez. { $reason }

# Message when anistream could not start because the config file has a setting it can't use. The path is the file; the problem names the line where it can.
start-failed-config = { $path } contient un réglage que anistream ne peut pas utiliser : { $problem }. Corrigez-le ou supprimez-le, puis réessayez.

# Message when anistream could not start because its database could not be opened. The path is the database file, the reason comes from the system.
start-failed-database = anistream n’a pas pu ouvrir sa base de données à { $path }. Si une autre application anistream est ouverte dans ce dossier, quittez-la, puis réessayez. { $reason }

# Message when anistream could not start its network connection from the network settings.
start-failed-network = anistream n’a pas pu configurer sa connexion réseau à partir des réglages réseau de config.toml. { $reason }

# Message when anistream itself could not start. The reason comes from the system or the engine.
start-failed = anistream n’a pas pu démarrer. Quittez-le et ouvrez-le à nouveau. { $reason }

# Message when the TV remote could not start listening or could not forget a phone.
start-failed-remote = La télécommande n’a pas pu démarrer. { $reason }

# Message when the built-in player could not start.
start-failed-player = Le lecteur n’a pas pu démarrer. { $reason }

# Toast after episodes are added to the download queue.
notice-episodes-queued =
    { $count ->
        [one] Un épisode ajouté à la file.
        [many] { $count } épisodes ajoutés à la file.
       *[other] { $count } épisodes ajoutés à la file.
    }

# Note under the connection-check group of the torrents dialog: what the check does.
torrents-linux-check-note = anistream vérifie par où sort le trafic des torrents au démarrage d’un torrent, puis chaque minute pendant son exécution, et met les torrents en pause si ce contrôle échoue. Votre VPN ou votre proxy est ce qui vous protège.

# Confirmation text when choosing "Warn only" for a failed check.
torrents-linux-warn-confirm = anistream vous avertira au lieu de mettre en pause. Si votre VPN ou votre proxy est coupé, d’autres personnes peuvent voir votre adresse IP.

# Status line once the protection has been checked and saved.
torrents-linux-protection-saved = Protection des torrents enregistrée

# Title of the dialog that turns torrents on.
torrents-linux-turn-on-title = Activer les torrents

# Title of the dialog that changes what protects torrents.
torrents-linux-protect-title = Protéger les torrents

# Title of the dialog that edits the proxy.
torrents-linux-edit-proxy-title = Modifier le proxy

# Button that turns torrents on in the dialog.
torrents-linux-turn-on-button = Activer

# Seeding row: time left until the goal, in a span already worded ("18h", "1d 6h").
downloads-linux-seed-left = { $span } restant

# Seeding row: less than an hour left until the goal.
downloads-linux-seed-left-soon = Moins d’une heure restante

# Storage row: free space, the disk's size and what downloads take. All three are sizes already formatted.
downloads-linux-space-free = { $free } libres sur { $total } · les téléchargements occupent { $taken }

# Placeholder of the search field. It also finds settings.
search-linux-placeholder = Rechercher titres et réglages

# Tooltip of the button that clears the recent searches.
search-linux-clear-recent = Effacer les recherches récentes

# Title of the state when a browse with no filters lists nothing.
search-linux-nothing-found = Aucun résultat

# Title of the state when a typed search waits for Enter.
search-linux-press-enter = Appuyez sur Entrée pour rechercher

# Line under the Enter title: why results do not come as you type. The tracker is a name.
search-linux-paused = La recherche pendant la saisie est suspendue un moment, pour respecter les limites de { $tracker }.

# Menu title over the sort choices of the filter row.
filter-linux-sort-by = Trier par

# Sort choice: what is rising now.
filter-linux-sort-trending = Tendances

# Sort choice: the most recent first.
filter-linux-sort-newest = Plus récents

# Sort choice: the earliest first.
filter-linux-sort-oldest = Plus anciens

# Sort choice: the most favourited first.
filter-linux-sort-favourites = Favoris

# Genre filter button when several genres are set.
filter-linux-genres-count =
    { $count ->
        [one] { $count } genre
        [many] { $count } genres
       *[other] { $count } genres
    }

# Format filter button when several formats are set.
filter-linux-formats-count =
    { $count ->
        [one] { $count } format
        [many] { $count } formats
       *[other] { $count } formats
    }

# Status filter button when several statuses are set.
filter-linux-statuses-count =
    { $count ->
        [one] { $count } statut
        [many] { $count } statuts
       *[other] { $count } statuts
    }

# Chip for a genre that is left out of the results. The genre is already named.
filter-linux-not = Sans { $genre }

# Button that takes off every filter chip.
filter-linux-clear-all = Tout effacer

# Tooltip of the arrow that scrolls the filter row back.
filter-linux-earlier = Filtres précédents

# Tooltip of the arrow that scrolls the filter row on.
filter-linux-more = Plus de filtres

# What a screen reader says for a broadcast whose time is an estimate. The time is already formatted.
calendar-linux-about = environ { $time }

# What a screen reader says for a broadcast that is the dub's.
calendar-linux-dubbed = doublé

# Title of the menu, and tooltip of its button, that orders a list.
library-linux-order = Ordre

# A list's tab: its name and how many titles it holds.
library-linux-list-count = { $list } { $count }

# Description read by a screen reader on the button that plays the shown episode on a TV.
title-linux-play-on-tv-help = Lire cet épisode sur une télévision avec anistream

# Description read by a screen reader on an episode's watched check box.
title-linux-episode-watched = Épisode { $episode } vu

# Line in a day's column when nothing airs that day.
calendar-linux-day-empty = Aucune diffusion

# Accessible label of the line that says how the watch party form is getting on.
party-status = Visionnage en groupe : état

# Accessible label of the list of people in the watch party, in the player's panel.
party-members = Membres

# Title of the dialog that lists the sources that have the watch party's episode.
party-choose-a-source = Choisir une source

# Line when no source lists the watch party's episode. A plugin store adds plugins, which add sources.
party-sources-none-listed = Aucune source ne liste l’épisode { $episode }. Les sources viennent des plugins, qu’une boutique de plugins ajoute.

# Line above the list of sources that have the watch party's episode.
party-sources-found-line =
    { $count ->
        [one] Une source l’a. Celle que vous choisissez se lit avec le visionnage en groupe.
        [many] { $count } sources l’ont. Celle que vous choisissez se lit avec le visionnage en groupe.
       *[other] { $count } sources l’ont. Celle que vous choisissez se lit avec le visionnage en groupe.
    }

# Notice when the player could not start, or could not be reached to add a track.
player-could-not-start = Le lecteur n’a pas pu démarrer. Réessayez, ou choisissez une autre source.

# Notice when the file chosen for a subtitle or audio track has no path the app can read.
player-file-unreadable = Impossible de lire ce fichier. Essayez-en un autre.

# The reason the system gives for keeping the screen awake and the computer from sleeping while an episode plays. Other apps and the desktop may show it.
player-inhibit-reason = Lecture d’un épisode

# Accessible description of the time left in the episode, beside the countdown.
player-time-left = Reste { $time }

# Line on the starting screen after a note from the engine, with the seconds waited.
player-note-waited = { $note } · { $seconds } s

# Starting screen's line before the episode is known.
player-starting-plain = Démarrage

# Tooltip of the Undo button on the card that says an opening was skipped. The letter is the key that does the same.
player-undo-tooltip = Annuler (U)

# Over the timeline: the time under the pointer, when it is inside an opening.
player-time-opening = { $clock } · Intro

# Over the timeline: the time under the pointer, when it is inside an ending.
player-time-ending = { $clock } · Générique

# Name of a one-channel audio track in the audio menu.
player-channels-mono = Mono

# Name of a two-channel audio track in the audio menu.
player-channels-stereo = Stéréo

# Name of an audio track with some other number of channels.
player-channels =
    { $count ->
        [one] Un canal
        [many] { $count } canaux
       *[other] { $count } canaux
    }

# Accessible label of the two buttons that switch between subbed and dubbed audio.
player-translation-label = Sous-titré ou doublé

# Tooltip on the button that opens a setting's preview on a page of its own, and accessible name of the preview.
settings-preview = Aperçu

# Tooltip on the button that steps a setting to its previous value.
settings-previous-value = Valeur précédente

# Tooltip on the button that steps a setting to its next value.
settings-next-value = Valeur suivante

# Line after the legal line under the sources settings: where sources come from.
settings-sources-come-from = Sources viennent des boutiques de plugins que vous rejoignez.

# Label on the left half of the upscaling preview: the video before processing.
settings-preview-source = Source 480p

# Preview note under the upscaling frame when upscaling is off.
settings-upscaling-note-off = La source 480p, mise à l’échelle sans traitement.

# A line of sample subtitle over the preview frame. Any short sentence will do.
settings-caption-sample = La route aux lanternes passe la dernière ville.

# Preview note under the subtitle frame. The language is a language name.
settings-caption-note = Les sous-titres simples s’affichent comme ceci, en { $language } quand un épisode en a. Les sous-titres stylisés gardent leur propre aspect.

# Preview note for new-episode notifications when they are on. The tracker is a name such as AniList.
settings-notify-note-on = Une notification quand un épisode d’une série de votre liste En cours sort, à l’heure donnée par { $tracker }. Le réglage propre à une série passe avant.

# Preview note for new-episode notifications when they are off.
settings-notify-note-off = Désactivé. Seules les séries activées dans leurs propres réglages envoient une notification.

# Heading of the preview note beside the sources settings while torrents are on.
settings-connection-check-title = Test de connexion

# Preview note beside the sources settings while torrents are on.
settings-connection-check-note = anistream vérifie par où sort le trafic des torrents au démarrage d’un torrent, puis chaque minute pendant qu’il tourne, et met les torrents en pause si ce contrôle échoue. C’est votre VPN ou votre proxy qui vous protège.

# Preview note beside the accounts settings.
settings-accounts-note = anistream fonctionne sans compte. Votre historique de visionnage reste sur cet ordinateur quand vous vous déconnectez.

# Preview note beside the Discord settings when presence is on.
settings-presence-note-on = Votre profil Discord affiche ce que vous regardez pendant la lecture d’un épisode.

# Preview note beside the Discord settings when presence is off.
settings-presence-note-off = Désactivé. Une fois activé, votre profil Discord affiche ce que vous regardez pendant la lecture d’un épisode.

# Preview note beside the advanced settings.
settings-advanced-note = Une option ici peut annuler un réglage de Lecture, comme la mise à l’échelle ou le mode nuit. La plupart des gens n’ont jamais besoin de ce volet.

# Button that opens the page of the new version of the app.
updates-view-version = Voir la version

# Accessible name of the progress bar while the new version downloads.
updates-progress-label = Progression de la mise à jour

# Line under AniList's name on the Accounts page.
accounts-sync-detail = La progression et les changements de liste se synchronisent avec { $tracker }. Bibliothèque et la liste du calendrier affichent vos listes { $tracker }.

# Line under a signed-in account while changes wait for the connection.
accounts-changes-waiting-offline =
    { $count ->
        [one] Un changement en attente de connexion
        [many] { $count } changements en attente de connexion
       *[other] { $count } changements en attente de connexion
    }

# Footnote on the Accounts page: where sign-in tokens are kept, when it is the system's keyring.
accounts-tokens-keyring = Les jetons de connexion sont conservés dans le trousseau de clés de cet appareil.

# Reason an update stopped: the downloaded file could not be read. The reason is the system's own words.
updates-why-read = Le téléchargement n’a pas pu être lu : { $reason }

# Reason an update stopped: the new version is in place but did not open.
updates-why-reopen = La nouvelle version est installée, mais elle n’a pas pu s’ouvrir. Relancez anistream.

# Accessible description of the mascot's picture. Nagare is the mascot's name.
nagare-description = Nagare, la mascotte de anistream : une silhouette au carré soyeux, une écharpe ambre et une cape indigo, tenant un bâton orné d’un talisman d’eau.

# Note under the Play trailers setting: what the trailers are and when they do not play.
settings-note-trailers-linux = Les bandes-annonces sont lues en sourdine depuis YouTube, qui voit votre adresse IP. Elles ne se lisent pas sur une connexion mesurée, avec les animations désactivées, en économie d’énergie ou avec un lecteur d’écran actif.

# Settings row: whether a connected game controller drives the app.
settings-label-controller-input = Utiliser une manette

# Settings row: swaps the A and B buttons, for a controller laid out as Nintendo's are.
settings-label-swap-face-buttons = Inverser A et B

# Heading of the Settings group for game controllers.
settings-group-controller = Manette

# Settings row that names the controller in use.
settings-controller-device = Manette

# Value of the controller row when no controller is connected.
settings-controller-none = Aucune manette détectée. Les dispositions clavier de Steam Input fonctionnent toujours.

# Notice when a controller connects for the first time in a session.
controller-connected = Manette connectée · { $name }

# Notice when the controller in use disconnects.
controller-disconnected = Manette déconnectée

# Title of the window that lists what the controller's buttons do.
controller-help-title = Manette

# Accessible name of the list of controller buttons in the help window.
controller-help-buttons = Boutons de la manette

# Button on a notice that asks to open the plugin stores.
shell-open-stores = Ouvrir les boutiques

# Button on an update notice that restarts the app to install it.
shell-restart = Redémarrer

# Button on a notice that a newer version is out: opens its page.
shell-view-release = Voir

# Notice when the app cannot keep running once its window is closed.
shell-no-background = anistream ne peut pas continuer de tourner en arrière-plan ici, donc les téléchargements s'arrêtent à la fermeture de la fenêtre.

# Tooltip of the main menu button in the sidebar's header.
shell-main-menu = Menu principal

# Sidebar line under a signed-out account: opens the accounts page to connect a tracker.
shell-connect-tracker = Connecter { $tracker }

# Sidebar line under the account when changes wait to be sent to the tracker.
shell-changes-waiting =
    { $count ->
        [one] Une modification à synchroniser
        [many] { $count } modifications à synchroniser
       *[other] { $count } modifications à synchroniser
    }

# Sidebar line under the account: the tracker, then that it is up to date.
shell-tracker-synced = { $tracker } · Synchronisé

# Heading of the shortcuts that work on lists of titles.
shortcuts-group-lists = Listes

# Shortcut: jump to a section of the app by number.
shortcuts-go-to-section = Aller à une section

# Shortcut: open the keyboard shortcuts window.
shortcuts-show = Raccourcis clavier

# Shortcut: close the window.
shortcuts-close-window = Fermer la fenêtre

# Shortcut: quit the app.
shortcuts-quit = Quitter

# Shortcut: play the title that has focus in a list.
shortcuts-play-selected = Lire le titre sélectionné

# Shortcut: small steps in the player.
shortcuts-seek-5 = Reculer ou avancer de 5 secondes

# Shortcut: larger steps in the player.
shortcuts-seek-30 = Reculer ou avancer de 30 secondes

# Shortcut: steps of ten seconds in the player.
shortcuts-seek-10 = Reculer ou avancer de 10 secondes

# Shortcut: change the volume.
shortcuts-volume = Monter ou baisser le volume

# Shortcut: skip the opening or the ending.
shortcuts-skip = Passer l'ouverture ou le générique de fin

# Shortcut: undo a skip the player made by itself.
shortcuts-undo-skip = Annuler un saut automatique

# Shortcut: change the playback speed.
shortcuts-speed = Accélérer ou ralentir

# Shortcut: answer the card that shows in the corner of the player.
shortcuts-answer-card = Répondre à la carte dans le coin

# Shortcut: Escape closes the topmost thing in the player, one step at a time.
shortcuts-escape = Fermer une carte, le mini-lecteur, le plein écran, puis le lecteur

# Response of the close question: stop what runs and close.
close-stop-and-close = Arrêter et fermer

# Body of the close question when episodes download.
close-body-downloading =
    { $count ->
        [one] Un épisode est en cours de téléchargement ou en attente. Le laisser continuer après la fermeture de la fenêtre, ou l'arrêter ?
        [many] { $count } épisodes sont en cours de téléchargement ou en attente. Les laisser continuer après la fermeture de la fenêtre, ou les arrêter ?
       *[other] { $count } épisodes sont en cours de téléchargement ou en attente. Les laisser continuer après la fermeture de la fenêtre, ou les arrêter ?
    }

# Body of the close question when episodes seed.
close-body-seeding =
    { $count ->
        [one] Un épisode est en cours de partage. Le laisser continuer après la fermeture de la fenêtre, ou l'arrêter ?
        [many] { $count } épisodes sont en cours de partage. Les laisser continuer après la fermeture de la fenêtre, ou les arrêter ?
       *[other] { $count } épisodes sont en cours de partage. Les laisser continuer après la fermeture de la fenêtre, ou les arrêter ?
    }

# Body of the close question when some episodes download and others seed.
close-body-both = Épisodes : { $downloading } en téléchargement ou en attente, et { $seeding } en partage. Les laisser continuer après la fermeture de la fenêtre, ou les arrêter ?

# Status in the sidebar and on the remote: the TV was not found again.
tv-status-not-found = { $name } introuvable

# Title of the dialog that wants a code to be typed: no name known yet.
tv-connecting-title = Connexion à la TV

# Heading of a problem when the pairing code ran out.
tv-code-expired = Code expiré

# Under a TV in the list: what choosing it does, for a screen reader.
tv-row-pairs-with = S'associe à cette TV

# Under a TV in the list: paired, but not seen on the network.
tv-row-away = Associée, pas vue sur ce réseau

# Under a TV in the list: found, not paired yet.
tv-row-new = Pas encore associée

# What a screen reader hears when a heading and its problem show together.
tv-problem-announce = { $heading }. { $problem }

# What a screen reader hears when no TV was found, then what to check.
tv-none-found-announce = Aucune TV trouvée. { $detail }

# Line on the picker while the episode to play is known: the show, then the episode.
tv-title-episode = { $title }, épisode { $episode }

# Line under the show on the remote and the picker: which episode.
tv-episode = Épisode { $episode }

# Line on the remote under the show: the episode, then its title.
tv-episode-titled = Épisode { $episode } · { $title }

# Explains the code a TV lists this computer by, above the paired TVs in the settings.
tv-fingerprint-note = Une TV affiche cet appareil avec le code { $code }. Si vous oubliez une TV ici, elle oublie aussi cet appareil.

# Settings line of a paired TV: paired on a date, reached in the last minute.
tv-paired-seen-now = { $paired } · vue à l'instant

# Accessible name of a track menu: the row, then the track chosen.
tv-track-choice = { $row }, { $track }

# The name this computer goes by in lists of a person's devices, such as a plugin store's.
shell-device-label = Ordinateur Linux

# Count of devices on a member's row in the members dialog, and after "Owner ·".
stores-device-count =
    { $count ->
        [one] { $count } appareil
        [many] { $count } appareils
       *[other] { $count } appareils
    }

# Accessible name of an owner's dialog: what the dialog does, then the plugin store it is for.
stores-dialog-title = { $title }, { $store }

# Title of the status page in an owner's dialog when the plugin store could not be reached. The reason is not shown here.
stores-owner-unreachable = Impossible de joindre la boutique de plugins

# Title of the status page in an owner's dialog when the plugin store did not answer in time.
stores-owner-no-answer = La boutique de plugins ne répond pas

# Line under it.
stores-owner-no-answer-detail = Elle est peut-être occupée, ou son ordinateur est éteint.

# Title of the status page in an owner's dialog when this device is offline.
stores-owner-needs-connection = La boutique de plugins nécessite une connexion

# Line under it.
stores-owner-needs-connection-detail = Réessayez quand cet appareil sera de nouveau connecté.

# Red line in the invite dialog when this device is offline and a link cannot be made.
stores-owner-link-offline = Créer un lien nécessite une connexion à la boutique de plugins.

# Line over a new invite link made for a named person. The time is the one the link stops working.
stores-send-link-until = Envoyez ce lien. Il fonctionne une seule fois, jusqu’au { $until }.

# Row title in who-can-join: switching on lets anyone with the link join. Shown while it is on.
stores-open-on-detail = Ils rejoignent sans nom. Désactiver cette option arrête le lien ; la réactiver en crée un nouveau.

# Row subtitle in who-can-join while it is off.
stores-open-off-detail = Seules les personnes que vous invitez peuvent rejoindre. Une fois activé, toute personne disposant du lien rejoint, sans nom.

# Line on the summary row of devices that joined with the link, when joining is on.
stores-open-no-names = Aucun nom n’est conservé.

# Line on the summary row of devices that joined with the link, when joining is off.
stores-open-keep-working = Ils continuent de fonctionner jusqu’à ce que vous les retiriez.

# Line under a device that joined with the link: when the store last saw it.
stores-device-seen = Vu { $when }

# Line under a device that joined with the link and has not been seen since.
stores-device-never-seen = Pas vu depuis son arrivée

# Short title of the publish dialog, over the plugin store's name.
stores-publish-short = Publier un plugin

# Line in the publish dialog when this device has no plugin to offer. Follows stores-publish-none.
stores-publish-none-hint = Un plugin que vous créez ou installez apparaît ici.

# Line under a plugin in the publish dialog that the store does not have yet.
stores-not-published = Pas encore dans la boutique de plugins

# Line under a plugin in the publish dialog that the store has in another version.
stores-store-offers = La boutique de plugins propose { $version }

# Line under a plugin in the publish dialog whose version the store already has.
stores-published-current = À jour dans la boutique de plugins

# Word at the end of that row.
stores-published-state = Publié

# Accessible name of a row's Publish button.
stores-publish-label = Publier { $name } { $version }

# Under a release in the source picker: how many people share it right now.
source-picker-seeders-linux =
    { $count ->
        [one] Un partageur
        [many] { $count } partageurs
       *[other] { $count } partageurs
    }

# Tooltip on the header bar button that shows the sidebar while the window is narrow.
sidebar-show = Afficher le menu

# Faint line over Continue's placeholders while it loads.
activity-continue = Chargement de ce que vous regardez

# Faint line over the calendar's placeholders while it loads.
activity-calendar = Chargement du calendrier

# Faint line over a title page's episode placeholders while they load.
activity-episodes = Chargement des épisodes

# Faint line over the Sources page while the sources are checked.
activity-sources = Vérification des sources

# Faint line over the Downloads page while it loads.
activity-downloads = Chargement des téléchargements

# Faint line over Search's placeholders while it lists titles with no query typed.
activity-browse = Chargement des titres

# A transfer rate: a size already worded, per second.
size-per-second = { $size }/s

# A wait that is over.
time-now = Maintenant

# How long ago, when it was inside the last minute.
time-just-now = À l’instant

# A length of time said for a screen reader, in hours.
spoken-hours =
    { $count ->
        [one] { $count } heure
        [many] { $count } heures
       *[other] { $count } heures
    }

# A length of time said for a screen reader, in minutes.
spoken-minutes =
    { $count ->
        [one] { $count } minute
        [many] { $count } minutes
       *[other] { $count } minutes
    }

# A length of time said for a screen reader, in seconds.
spoken-seconds =
    { $count ->
        [one] { $count } seconde
        [many] { $count } secondes
       *[other] { $count } secondes
    }

# Continue row: nothing new to watch, and the next episode airs at a known time. The time is already worded: "in 2d 3h".
continue-row-caught-up-airs = À jour · E{ $episode } sort { $when }

# Continue row: nothing new to watch, and the next episode has no date.
continue-row-caught-up-not-out = À jour · E{ $episode } n’est pas encore sorti

# Name of a language, in a list of subtitle languages.
